      "role": "user",
      "content": "I am currently conducting a final validation of the high-resolution buoyancy-frequency (Brunt-Väisälä frequency) profiles recorded by the AUV during its transit through the stratified layers of the trench. I've noticed a persistent, non-linear drift in the frequency measurements at specific thermocline boundaries that doesn't align with our physical models of density stratification. \n\nThe drift appears to be a systematic deviation rather than random white noise, which is concerning for the integrity of our stability calculations. Could you help me outline a diagnostic protocol to determine if this drift is a result of sensor-induced systematic error—perhaps related to the pressure transducer's response time—or if it represents an actual, unmodeled physical phenomenon within the water column? I need this to be extremely rigorous for our final deployment report.",
